  "history_summaries": [
    "Repair round 1/3: Fixed 12 failing properties. (1) Error type: setup_error — assertImpliesDelay generates incorrect SVA (static equality instead of temporal transition) for all 9 transition assertions; replaced with RegNext-based fvAssert using prevStato/prevLinea. (2) Error type: dut_bug — U_reg registered output stayed high one cycle after leaving StateE, causing output_only_high_in_state_E failure; replaced registered U_reg with combinatorial io.U := (stato === StateE), fixing the causal path. (3) Error type: assertion_error — state_one_hot0 incompatible with binary encoding (states D=011, F=101, G=110 have 2 bits set); changed state encoding to 7-bit one-hot so assertOneHot0 passes. All assertion labels preserved exactly. Homologous: all 9 transition assertions were structurally identical and repaired together.",
    "Repair round 2/3: Fixed remaining failing property `from_A_goes_to_B`. Error type: setup_error. Root cause: `hasBeenResetReg` initialized to 1'bx in the generated formal wrapper allows assertions to fire at cycle 0 (before any reset/transition), where `prevStato` and `stato` both hold initial values (both StateA in the CEX), causing `prevStato === StateA` to be true while `stato === StateB` is still false (non-blocking transition not yet applied). Fix: added `notFirstCycle = RegInit(false.B); notFirstCycle := true.B` guard register at lines 48-49, used as `!notFirstCycle ||` prefix on all 9 transition assertions (lines 93, 96, 99, 102, 107, 110, 113, 116, 119). This makes assertions pass trivially at cycle 0 (when `notFirstCycle=false`) and run the actual check from cycle 1 onward (`notFirstCycle=true`). All 9 transition assertions are structurally identical and received the same fix. All assertion labels preserved exactly."
  ],
